{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-minus-layers-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T22:17:21.071Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"cfa40d6a9e3c1b1347f2d170ff6b5f68b12672ac723e40637780c183324189ca","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from *Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth* (`teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md`). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at the gatehouse kiosk for Dock Doors 14–18 at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their bay assignments by text. Support patched the text-message routing that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the 04:00 shift got through without anyone stepping in by hand.\n2. **#4419**, from *Moss: North cheat sheet* (`teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md`). This note has no date. Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 product support so they could test the scanner firmware.\n\nThe note writes it as \"#4419\" with no PD- prefix. I've left it as written rather than guess at the format.\n\n**No ticket numbers in Moss's other notes:**\n- The 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest mentions Quarrendon, but only for call prep on appointment time vs. gate arrival.\n- The 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in only covers the renewal signing.\n- The Central team notes list #4409, #4412 and FR-882. Those belong to Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon.\n\nMoss's North cheat sheet warns not to mix up Quarrendon Freight Lines with Quarendon Freightways, which uses a competitor's software and isn't a customer. Nothing above is from Freightways.\n\nI looked at the Moss notes you have access to, and Moss hasn't posted in #general or #help-it-ops."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
